    category: "Linux",
    title: "多主流 Linux 發行版發布安全更新：涵蓋核心、Web 服務與多個應用層元件",
    summary: "多個主要的 Linux 發行版，包括 AlmaLinux、Debian、Fedora、Mageia、Oracle、SUSE 和 Ubuntu，近期發布了廣泛的安全性更新。這些更新涵蓋了從作業系統核心（kernel）到各種應用層函式庫和服務的廣泛範圍。具體受影響的元件包括：AlmaLinux 更新了 assertj-core、golang、httpd、kernel 和 libxml2；Debian 更新了 chromium 和 suricata-update；Fedora 更新了 rust-h2；Oracle 針對 kernel、mingw-openssl 等進行修補；而 SUSE 和 Ubuntu 則分別針對大量核心元件和應用程式進行了更新，例如 SUSE 更新了 openssl、openssl-3、rsync、java-11-openjdk 等，而 Ubuntu 更新了多個與雲端和特定平台相關的 Linux 模組（如 linux-azure、linux-gcp-fips 等）。這些更新的實務影響是確保系統在面對各種已知漏洞時，能夠維持穩定的安全狀態。資安人員和系統管理員應根據發行版的官方公告，及時更新所有列出的核心元件和應用程式，以修補潛在的漏洞，維持系統的安全性。",
    tags: ["Linux", "AlmaLinux", "Debian", "Fedora", "SUSE", "Ubuntu", "Kernel", "安全更新"],
    title_en: "Multiple Major Linux Distributions Release Security Updates: Covering Kernel, Web Services, and Multiple Application Components",
    summary_en: "Several major Linux distributions, including AlmaLinux, Debian, Fedora, Mageia, Oracle, SUSE, and Ubuntu, recently released extensive security updates. These updates cover a wide range of components, from the operating system kernel to various application-layer libraries and services. Specific affected components include: AlmaLinux updated assertj-core, golang, httpd, kernel, and libxml2; Debian updated chromium and suricata-update; Fedora updated rust-h2; Oracle patched kernel, mingw-openssl, and others; while SUSE and Ubuntu updated numerous core components and applications. For example, SUSE updated openssl, openssl-3, rsync, and java-11-openjdk, and Ubuntu updated multiple Linux modules related to cloud and specific platforms (such as linux-azure and linux-gcp-fips). The practical impact of these updates is ensuring that systems maintain a stable security posture when facing various known vulnerabilities. Security personnel and system administrators should promptly update all listed core components and applications according to the official announcements of their respective distributions to patch potential vulnerabilities and maintain system security.",
    tags_en: ["Linux", "AlmaLinux", "Debian", "Fedora", "SUSE", "Ubuntu", "Kernel", "Security Update"],
