    title_en: "Canonical Releases Ubuntu 26.04.1 Point Update, Providing Upgrade Path for 24.04 LTS Users",
    summary_en: "Canonical has released Ubuntu 26.04.1, the first point release update for this year's Long Term Support (LTS) version. This version is supported until 2031 and signals that Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (Noble Numbat) users will begin receiving notifications to upgrade to the new version. This update is not limited to graphical desktop users; server users will also be notified through the output messages of the `apt` command. The article notes that in addition to the official eight-point release, Pop!_OS 26.04 is also expected soon, which will utilize the built-in COSMIC desktop environment. The COSMIC desktop environment is rapidly developing, with new versions (such as 1.7.0) showing faster performance than standard Ubuntu and demonstrating potential in supporting both older hardware and modern kernels. Developers should pay attention to the development trends of these new versions and desktop environments.",
