    title_en: "iOS 27 Major Upgrade: Apple Photos and iCloud Shared Albums Feature Improvements Support Full-Resolution Content and Cross-Platform Collaboration",
    summary_en: "This article introduces major feature upgrades to Apple Photos within the iOS 27 operating system, focusing specifically on 'iCloud Shared Albums.' With the upgrade, the shared album functionality has been significantly enhanced, now supporting full-resolution photos and videos, meeting users' demand for high-quality shared content. Furthermore, user interaction has been improved; in addition to the traditional 'Like,' users can now react using any emoji. One of the biggest improvements is that Android and Windows users can now contribute content to shared albums via the web interface, a feature previously limited to Apple users. Other optimizations include more convenient saving of shared photos, setting new participant permissions, and even the option to set the album to automatically expire on a specific date. These improvements make the shared album experience feel closer to a complete social sharing platform, making it one of the key highlights of iOS 27.",
