    summary_en: "Google has released Android 17 QPR2 Beta 4 for Pixel devices. This Beta 4 version has achieved Platform Stability, primarily fixing multiple system-level and User Interface (UI) bugs. Fixes include resolving the issue where the launcher status bar became transparent after full-screen video playback; fixing errors that caused unexpected device reboots due to thermal management issues; and improving unresponsiveness when gesture navigation rendered applications below the display cutout. Furthermore, system optimizations covered battery restrictions, application drawer search failures, and the inability to use the microphone due to audio service resource locking. This update also introduces status bar customization. Users are advised to participate in testing via the Android Beta Program to ensure system stability and to monitor official announcements regarding the support lifespan for the Pixel 11 series.",
