    summary_en: "This article provides a detailed comparison of the hardware and software specifications of the Google Pixel 11 and the Pixel 11 Pro. While the two models share a highly similar aesthetic design, the Pro model maintains advantages in display, camera, and connectivity. The Pixel 11 Pro features a higher-resolution 1280 x 2856 display, a peak brightness of 3,600 nits, and a dedicated anti-scratch coating. Furthermore, the Pro model supports Wi-Fi 7 and UWB, and includes the HiLight feature. In terms of storage, the high-end configuration of the Pro model offers Zoned UFS storage and can be upgraded up to 16GB of RAM. Both models are expected to support up to seven years of OS and security updates and are equipped with Gemini AI features, including proactive task offloading and optimized voice input for Gboard. Regarding the camera, the Pixel 11 upgrades to a 48MP main sensor, representing an improvement over its predecessor. In terms of battery, the base Pixel 11 has a slightly larger capacity (4,985 mAh) compared to the Pro model (4,850 mAh).",
