    title_en: "Apple TV launches 'Dark Matter' Season 2, sci-fi thriller focuses on parallel dimensions and family crisis",
    summary_en: "Apple TV has announced the launch of 'Dark Matter' Season 2. This sci-fi thriller continues the storyline from Season 1, following a physicist in Chicago who is kidnapped and awakens in a parallel version of his life. This season will focus on the Dessens family, who face unimaginable crises in what appears to be a peaceful life. The plot will delve into the characters' psychological stress, such as Daniela (Jennifer Connelly)'s growing paranoia, and their son Charlie (Oakes Fegley)'s longing for stability. Furthermore, Amanda (Alice Braga) and Ryan (Jimmi Simpson) will be forced to join forces to find their way home, while Blair (Amanda Brugel) and Leighton (Dayo Okeniyi) will each push them toward a grand vision of a perfect world. The series is adapted from Blake Crouch's 2016 novel of the same name. Viewers can watch the show on Apple TV for $12.99 per month or as part of the Apple One bundle. This content is for film and entertainment information and contains no technical vulnerabilities or cybersecurity risks.",
