    summary_en: "Meta announced a new firmware update for Ray-Ban Smart Glasses and Meta Smart Glasses to further enhance the detection capability of the privacy LED. This update aims to address a previously existing vulnerability: users could obscure the LED after recording had started, thereby bypassing system restrictions. The new mechanism will ensure that if the light is detected as being obscured (whether through physical tampering, covering, or damage), the camera will automatically stop recording. Meta stated that this continuous update will improve the reliability of the \"Capture LED,\" ensuring that bystanders in the vicinity can reliably know when photos or videos are being taken. Furthermore, the privacy page on the Meta website emphasizes that photos and videos taken can only be viewed by the user themselves, differing from previous reports that mentioned human reviewers viewing the footage. This update is released amid high public scrutiny of smart glasses, aiming to elevate the level of user privacy protection.",
