    summary_en: "OpenAI has confirmed updates to the plugin functionality of ChatGPT and Codex, now supporting the connection of multiple Gmail, Google Calendar, and Google Contacts accounts. Previously, each plugin could only connect to a single Google account, limiting users' application scope when handling personal and work account data. This update allows users to use different accounts within the same ChatGPT interface to manage personal emails, work schedules, or contact information. This enables ChatGPT to extract relevant information from multiple connected accounts, providing more comprehensive and context-aware responses, significantly enhancing its utility in both personal and professional settings. Users can add accounts for connected services (such as Gmail) by clicking the gear icon on the plugin settings page. However, OpenAI documentation also reminds users that connected accounts remain subject to their respective application permissions and workspace controls, and actual usability will vary depending on the user's subscription plan, organizational policies, and administrator settings.",
