    category: "重點關注",
    title: "中國稀土出口管制令數據中心面臨衝擊，關鍵材料供應鏈面臨不確定性",
    summary: "根據 IEEE Spectrum 的報導，中國對稀土礦物的出口管制，特別是針對 IT 設備所需的<0xE9><0x90><0xBF>（yttrium）和<0xE9><0x95><0xB1>（erbium）這兩種稀土元素，正使全球數據中心面臨潛在的供應鏈風險。中國自 2025 年起已實施多輪限制，包括要求公司必須取得許可證才能出口含有中國來源稀土的產品。目前，<0xE9><0x90><0xBF>和<0xE9><0x95><0xB1>在白 LED 照明、顯示器、微波濾波器和光纖鏈路放大器等電子設備中用途廣泛，且中國在這些材料的採礦、分離和精煉環節幾乎壟斷了全球供應。雖然美國等國家已啟動多項投資（如國防部和能源部）以分散供應鏈，並簽署了多國協議，但中國預計在今年十一月將重新評估其出口政策，其最終決定將對全球關鍵礦物市場構成重大不確定性。",
    tags: ["稀土礦物", "中國", "數據中心", "供應鏈", "<0xE9><0x90><0xBF>", "<0xE9><0x95><0xB1>", "出口管制"],
    title_en: "China's Rare Earth Export Controls Threaten Data Centers and Create Supply Chain Uncertainty for Key Materials",
    summary_en: "According to a report by IEEE Spectrum, China's export controls on rare earth minerals, particularly targeting yttrium and erbium—elements crucial for IT equipment—are posing potential supply chain risks to global data centers. China has implemented multiple rounds of restrictions since 2025, including requiring companies to obtain permits to export products containing China-sourced rare earths. Yttrium and erbium are widely used in electronic devices such as white LED lighting, displays, microwave filters, and optical fiber link amplifiers. Furthermore, China has maintained a near-monopoly on the global supply chain for the mining, separation, and refining of these materials. Although countries like the United States have initiated various investments (such as from the Department of Defense and the Department of Energy) to diversify supply chains and have signed multilateral agreements, China is expected to re-evaluate its export policies this November. Its final decision will introduce significant uncertainty into the global critical mineral market.",
    tags_en: ["Rare Earth Minerals", "China", "Data Centers", "Supply Chain", "Yttrium", "Erbium", "Export Controls"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/systems/2026/08/28/datacenters-face-direct-hit-from-china-rare-earth-curbs-as-clock-runs-out-on-escalated-licensing-chokeoff/5293257", lang: "EN" }
    ]
